# Ingenium invariants (break one = card rejected)

1. Git: read-only. No checkout, reset, stash, commit, rebase, push, or any history change without Tope's explicit yes.
2. Formatters: only the repo's Prettier/ESLint/Ruff. Never reformat a file you are not changing.
3. Databases: disposable `ingenium_*` only. Drop what you create. Never touch client or production DBs. Never wipe stacks you did not create. Never weaken `assert_isolated()` or the docker guard.
4. Plain language: every owner-visible word follows the glossary (handover Appendix C). The jargon guard must pass.
5. Preserve every feature: before removing or merging anything, list what it did and where it now lives. Retirements need Tope's yes.
6. Ideas outside SPEC, CONFIG_SUITE_SPEC, BRIDGE_RUNNER_SPEC, FEATURE_AUDIT, or DESIGN_TOUCHES are proposals, not builds.
7. Evidence or it did not happen: log date, command, result, and label in `apps/api/evals/v2/PROGRESS.md`.
8. Never invent facts. Label inferences `[Inferred]`. Never upgrade a label without new evidence.
9. FOSS only (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC, MPL-2.0, LGPL dynamic, PostgreSQL). No ELv2, SSPL, BSL, Commons Clause, or unlicensed code.
10. One change at a time, verified (unit, then live).
11. Leave the machine as found. Stop only your own processes. Never take ports 3002, 8001, 8002, 8012, 5433, 5436, 8069-8073, or 11434.
12. Clean-room: public ORM/RPC only. No direct SQL on client DBs. Never read Enterprise Studio source.
13. AI proposes, code authorises. No model output reaches `execute_kw`, an install, or an exported module without a deterministic validator.
14. Money guard and write gate: changed only by L3-routed cards with Elite design notes, locked oracle tests, and a separate L3 Reviewer.
15. Honest data: every number on screen comes from the connected DB or is labelled "Example".
16. `evals/v2/holdout_fresh/` stays sealed: never read its gold or tune against it.
17. Never log or paste secrets or client PII (logs, packets, evidence, screenshots).
18. Destructive or external actions (deletes, migrations, installs on non-disposable DBs, outbound sends, pushes) need Tope's explicit yes in the current message.

Repo traps: `:8001` runs without `--reload`, so do not restart it. A bare `next build` overwrites dev `.next` (use your own `distDir`). Views use `<tree>` on 17 and `<list>` on 18+. No `attrs`. No positional xpath. Odoo 20 uses `ir.access` and has no `ir.rule`. AI calls go only through `app/ai_client`, with untrusted text in `fence_fields`. UI uses tokens only (no raw hex). Light-ish backgrounds get dark ink.
